## The two fixes

F49 (X-P8-12): `storytimeCardMatchSource` in `dashboard/lib/storytime/print/card-kit.ts` read the third column of a match line with `fields[2] ?? ''`. A line with fewer than three columns had an empty third column, so the function returned `picture`. The fix returns `none` when the third column is missing or empty. `storytimeCardMatchCounts` uses that function, so it counts such a line as `none`. The JSDoc of both functions names the rule.

F50 (X-P8-13): `stickerCentre` in the same file read `centres[label]`. The centre map is a plain object, so a label such as `constructor`, `toString`, or `__proto__` returned an inherited member, and `raw.trim()` threw. The fix reads the centre only when `Object.hasOwn(centres, label)` holds. A label without an own key prints at the default centre `50% 50%`. The values of `STORYTIME_STICKER_CENTER_OVERRIDES` and the sticker layout stay the same.

The two `it.fails` markers of X-P8-12 (line 311) and X-P8-13 (line 445) in `dashboard/__tests__/storytime-print-card-kit-adversarial-r2.test.ts` are now `it`. The precedent is commit 03e20aac, which did the same for X-P8-10 and X-P8-11. No other line of any test file changed.

